text:
maria: Customer on Dedicated reported huge spike in latency and a burst of 500/401s after a token refresh kicked in. They say SDK retried several times and we saw multiple /v1/generate calls for the same request.
sam: Which SDK + undici versions? Node version?
tyler: Any chance they're reusing an AbortController across retries? that's a common footgun.
maria: They sent a small repro: Node 20, @redwood-js 0.18.2, undici 5.20.2. Using our TS SDK with automatic retries enabled. They said token refresh happens on 401 and the refresh path calls the same client with a new token.
jordan: Can you paste the minimal repro snippet? also logs would help.
maria: Repro (sanitized):
```
// simplified
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: getToken() });
async function send() {
  const ac = new AbortController();
  const res = await client.generate({ prompt }, { signal: ac.signal });
}
// token refresher: on 401 we fetch new token and retry original call by invoking send() again
```
They said they do a programmatic retry (call send again) inside our SDK retry hook. Logs:
```
REQUEST id=abc123 START
REQUEST id=abc123 REATTEMPT 1 (401)
TOKEN REFRESH START
TOKEN REFRESH DONE
REQUEST id=abc123 START
REQUEST id=abc123 ERROR 500 upstream
REQUEST id=abc123 REATTEMPT 2
```
maria: They see 3 distinct network calls for the same logical request and latency goes from 200ms to 2.4s. Also downstream billing counters increment per attempt.
sam: Sounds like two interacting retry layers: their manual re-call on 401 plus SDK's automatic retry/backoff + undici internal behavior. If AbortController is reused across attempts it can be signaled and cause weird immediate cancellations
tyler: Undici's fetch semantics in Node 20 changed. Also undici <=5.20 had some signal handoff quirks. Recommend upgrading undici and our SDK to latest patch first.
jordan: For a short-term mitigation: disable SDK auto-retries for this client or ensure token refresh path returns a promise that resolves before SDK retry kicks in. Also generate idempotency keys for requests where possible.
maria: Customer wants a reproducible minimal repro that we can run. I built a tiny script that simulates token rotation + overlapping retries.
```
// repro test
let token = 't1';
async function getToken() { return token; }
async function refreshToken() { token = 't2'; }
// call path
try {
  await client.generate({ prompt }, { signal: (new AbortController()).signal });
} catch (e) {
  if (e.status === 401) { await refreshToken(); await client.generate({ prompt }); }
}
```
maria: They said when we add a small jitter before the retry (100-300ms) the duplicate calls drop and latency stabilizes.
sam: Can we add guidance in support playbook: "Never reuse AbortController across SDK retries; prefer per-call signals. If you implement token refresh on 401, coordinate with SDK retry (disable automatic retries during refresh)." add links to code snippets.
tyler: I'll open an eng-runtime ticket to look at SDK retry+auth handshake ordering and consider making token-refresh hook pluggable so SDK can pause retries while refresh is in-flight. @eng-runtime-bot can you create an issue?
eng-runtime-bot: created RED-issue-4821 "investigate SDK retry/auth race causing duplicate requests and latency regressions" assigned to @tyler
jordan: Also add a recommended quick fix for customers: bump undici to >=5.21.0, set SDK retry.maxAttempts=1 while token refresh is being implemented, and use per-request AbortController.
maria: I'll send the customer a concise troubleshooting email with the steps and ask them to try patching undici & toggling retries. I'll attach the repro script and logs.
sam: Thanks — if they still hit duplicates we'll escalate with full traces.
maria: @tyler please keep us posted on the ticket, customer is sensitive because it's affecting their Dedicated bill. :frowning:
